PopGB - License
===============

PopGB is an unofficial port of the gnuboy Game Boy / Game Boy Color
emulator to the SHARP Brain PW-G5300 (Windows CE, ARM). Its license
has two levels.

1. PopGB as a whole: the GNU GPL, version 2 (same terms as upstream)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

PopGB as a whole (AppMain.exe, and the source published in this
repository) is distributed under the GNU General Public License,
version 2 (GPL-2.0), on the same terms as upstream gnuboy. The full
text of the GPL version 2 is in COPYING at the repository root.

This file does not state whether a later version of the GPL may also
be chosen: the upstream files are not consistent about it. gnuboy's
main.c (section 3 below) and some sys/sdl/ and sys/sdl2/ files say
"version 2, or (at your option) any later version"; others only say
"GNU GPL", sys/thinlib/ (not built) says LGPL version 2, and most of
the core files built into AppMain.exe carry no license notice of their
own. See sys/ce/LICENSING.md, section 1.

The GPL allows redistribution, including commercial use, on its terms:
keep the license and the copyright notices, make the corresponding
source available with any binary, and keep derived works as a whole
under the GPL. There is no warranty.

2. PopGB's own code: MIT
----------------------------------------------------------------------

This MIT license covers only PopGB's own code listed in
sys/ce/LICENSING.md (the files marked "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT":
the sys/ce/ frontend except the font data, the mascot image and the icon,
sys/ce/tools/, and Makefile.ce). PopGB as a whole is distributed under
the GPL (section 1).

